# KIRIN NEOVIM — INTERACTIVE BASICS

You can also run `:Tutor` to open Neovim's full original introduction.

## Moving the cursor *movement*

Use `h`, `j`, `k`, `l` to move. `0` goes to the line start; `$` to its end; `w` to the next word.

Use `cw` to turn WRONG into READY here:

WRONG [[READY]]

## Entering text *insert*

Use `i` to enter Insert mode and `<Esc>` to return to Normal mode.

Put the word Kirin after the colon:

Editor: [[Editor: Kirin]]

## Undo and redo *undo*

Use `u` to undo, `<C-r>` to redo. Try editing this line:

This line is safe to edit. [[-1]]

## Saving and getting help *help*

`:w` saves the buffer; `:q` quits; `:q!` discards changes.

Use `:help tutor` or `:help motion.txt` to learn more. Back at a shell, try `kirin-learn learn editors`.
